window.__PHD.push(" & Production Teaching and Research Office, Quanzhou Huaguang College, China\\nPortfolio & CV: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\", \"note_zh\": \"\u5207\u5165\u70b9\uff1aFingerMapper \u5c0f\u624b\u6307\u2192\u5927\u52a8\u4f5c\uff0c\u6b63\u5408\u5c55\u67dc\u524d\u6709\u9650\u7a7a\u95f4\uff1b\u4ed6\u662f\u8bbe\u8ba1\u5e08\u51fa\u8eab\uff08\u524d Centre Pompidou IRI\uff09\u3001HDR\uff0c\u5bf9\u8bbe\u8ba1\u80cc\u666f\u6700\u53cb\u597d\u3002\u53d1\u9001\u524d\u6838\u5b9e\uff1aT\u00e9l\u00e9com Paris/IP Paris \u7684 CSC \u9014\u5f84\uff08JSON \u5f52\u5165 ParisTech \u4f46\u672a\u786e\u8ba4\uff09\uff1bJSON \u65e0\u90ae\u7bb1\uff0c\u9700\u4ece T\u00e9l\u00e9com Paris \u9875\u9762\u67e5\u3002\"}, \"unit_zh\": \"SES \u7cfb / \u8de8\u5b66\u79d1\u521b\u65b0\u7814\u7a76\u6240\uff08i3\uff0cCNRS UMR 9217\uff09\uff0cInteract \u4e0e DIVA \u56e2\u961f\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Pierre Cubaud\", \"school_en\": \"Conservatoire national des arts et m\u00e9tiers (Cnam), Paris\", \"school_zh\": \"\u6cd5\u56fd\u56fd\u7acb\u5de5\u827a\u5b66\u9662\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Professeur des universit\u00e9s (CE1)\uff1bCEDRIC \u5b9e\u9a8c\u5ba4 Interactivit\u00e9 pour lire et jouer (ILJ) \u56e2\u961f\u8054\u5408\u521b\u59cb\u4eba\uff1b2014\u201319 \u4efb CEDRIC \u4e3b\u4efb\", \"unit\": \"CEDRIC (EA 4629) \u2013 ILJ\", \"homepage\": \"https://cedric.cnam.fr/en/author/cubaud\", \"email\": \"cubaud@cnam.fr\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cC\u68af\u961f\u3011\u535a\u7269\u9986\u4e2d\u4ecb/\u5b9e\u4f53\u53ef\u611f\u77e5\u4ea4\u4e92\u4e0e\u6587\u5316\u9057\u4ea7\u6570\u5b57\u5316\u662f\u4ed6\u957f\u671f\u65b9\u5411\uff0c\u66fe\u505a\u535a\u7269\u9986 AR \u5bfc\u89c8\uff0c\u5e76\u4e0e\u8bbe\u8ba1\u5b66\u6821 ENSCI \u5408\u529e\u7855\u58eb\uff1b\u4f46\u4ed6\u8fd1\u5e74\u805a\u7126\u4e00\u4e2a\u6559\u80b2\u7528\u5b9e\u4f53\u8ba1\u7b97\u673a\u9879\u76ee\uff0c\u4e0d\u505a\u624b\u52bf\u4e0e\u706f\u5149\uff0c\u7814\u7a76\u4ea7\u51fa\u8f83\u5c11\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://cedric.cnam.fr/en/author/cubaud\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"A Tangible Computer for Science Museums: Pilot Machine\", \"year\": 2025, \"venue\": \"Technical report, Cnam / Universcience (HAL hal-05431090)\", \"url\": \"https://hal.science/hal-05431090\", \"link_to_user\": \"\", \"title_zh\": \"\u9762\u5411\u79d1\u5b66\u535a\u7269\u9986\u7684\u6709\u5f62\u8ba1\u7b97\u673a\uff1a\u8bd5\u70b9\u88c5\u7f6e\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://cedric.cnam.fr/en/author/cubaud\", \"https://cedric.cnam.fr/~cubaud/cvcubaud25FR.pdf\", \"https://cedric.cnam.fr/teams/ilj-en\", \"https://hal.science/hal-05431090\", \"https://www.irill.org/events/2026/event20260521.html\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"cubaud@cnam.fr\", \"subject\": \"CSC-funded PhD enquiry (2027 entry): gesture-driven light for museum mediation\", \"body\": \"Dear Professor Cubaud,\\n\\nI recently read your report \\\"A Tangible Computer for Science Museums: Pilot Machine\\\" (2025). Your marble-based stored-program machine, which makes the internal operations of a computer accessible to museum visitors, and the modifications suggested by its public presentations, struck me as a clear case of mediation through physical, perceivable processes rather than screens. My own heritage prototypes still rely on a screen, and I would like to move the interaction into the exhibition space itself, using visitors' gestures to drive programmable light. Your earlier work on augmented reality guides for museum visits is also close to this question.\\n\\nI hope to start a PhD in autumn 2027 at the Cnam, funded by the China Scholarship Council (CSC) through its national government-sponsored programme. Would you be willing to consider supervising me in the CEDRIC laboratory's Interactivit\u00e9 pour lire et jouer team, and might you have capacity for a new doctoral student in 2027?\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\uff0810-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u53d1\u9001\uff0c\u53d1\u524d\u9010\u5c01\u786e\u8ba4\u3002\"}, \"title_zh\": \"\u5927\u5b66\u6559\u6388\uff08Professeur des universit\u00e9s\uff0cCE1\uff09\uff1bCEDRIC \u5b9e\u9a8c\u5ba4\u201c\u9605\u8bfb\u4e0e\u6e38\u620f\u4ea4\u4e92\u6027\u201d\uff08ILJ\uff09\u56e2\u961f\u8054\u5408\u521b\u59cb\u4eba\uff1b2014\u201319 \u4efb CEDRIC \u4e3b\u4efb\", \"unit_zh\": \"CEDRIC\uff08EA 4629\uff09\u2013 ILJ \u56e2\u961f\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Susanne Boll\", \"school_en\": \"Carl von Ossietzky Universit\u00e4t Oldenburg\", \"school_zh\": \"\u5965\u5c14\u767b\u5821\u5927\u5b66\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Prof. Dr. techn.\uff0cFull Professor of Media Informatics and Multimedia Systems\uff08\u81ea 2013 \u8d77\u6b63\u6559\u6388\uff09\uff1bOFFIS \u4fe1\u606f\u6280\u672f\u7814\u7a76\u6240\u8463\u4e8b\u4f1a\u6210\u5458\", \"unit\": \"Department of Computing Science, Media Informatics and Multimedia Systems Group, University of Oldenburg\", \"homepage\": \"https://uol.de/en/media-informatics/team/susanne-boll\", \"email\": \"Susanne.Boll@informatik.uni-oldenburg.de\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cB\u68af\u961f\u3011\u5fb7\u56fd\u552f\u4e00\u540c\u65f6\u505a\u300c\u7a7a\u4e2d\u624b\u52bf\u8bbe\u8ba1\uff08GrIPSs, CHI'23/'24\uff09\u300d\u548c\u300c\u73af\u5883\u5149/\u5149\u663e\u793a\u300d\u7684 HCI \u7ec4\uff0c\u6070\u597d\u8986\u76d6\u7528\u6237 RQ2\uff08\u6587\u5316\u5316\u7684\u624b\u52bf\u2013\u706f\u5149\u6620\u5c04\uff09\u4e0e\u53ef\u7f16\u7a0b\u5b9e\u4f53\u5149\u4e24\u5927\u652f\u67f1\uff1b\u65b9\u6cd5\u4e0a\u7528 elicitation/\u7528\u6237\u7814\u7a76\uff0c\u4e0e RtD+\u5bf9\u7167\u5b9e\u9a8c\u76f8\u5bb9\u3002\u7f3a\u53e3\uff1a\u65e0\u535a\u7269\u9986/\u6587\u5316\u9057\u4ea7\u9879\u76ee\uff0c\u8fd1\u5e74\u5149\u663e\u793a\u8bba\u6587\u591a\u5728 2019 \u524d\uff0c\u4e14\u91cd\u5fc3\u504f\u6c7d\u8f66/\u5065\u5eb7\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://uol.de/en/media-informatics/team/susanne-boll\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"Controlling the Rooms: How People Prefer Using Gestures to Control Their Smart Homes\", \"year\": 2024, \"venue\": \"CHI '24 (Proceedings of the 2024 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems), Article 550\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642687\", \"link_to_user\": \"\", \"title_zh\": \"\u63a7\u5236\u623f\u95f4\uff1a\u4eba\u4eec\u5982\u4f55\u504f\u597d\u7528\u624b\u52bf\u63a7\u5236\u667a\u80fd\u5bb6\u5c45\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://uol.de/en/media-informatics/team/susanne-boll\", \"https://uol.de/en/media-informatics\", \"https://uol.de/en/media-informatics/jobs\", \"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3613904.3642687\", \"https://scalableinteractionparadigms.uni-oldenburg.de/blog/gestural-interaction-paradigms-for-smart-spaces-gripss/\", \"https://uol.de/informatik/studium-lehre/promotion\", \"https://uol.de/f/6/Promotion/Dr._rer._nat/FK_II_V_VI_Lesefassung_Gemeinsame_Promotionsordnung_FKII_FKV_FKVI_01.08.2022_EN.pdf\", \"https://uol.de/informatik/department/gremien-beauftragte/gremien/promotionsausschuss/promotionsordnung\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"Susanne.Boll@informatik.uni-oldenburg.de\", \"subject\": \"CSC-funded PhD enquiry (2027 entry): Mid-air gestures and programmable light in heritage exhibitions\", \"body\": \"Dear Professor Boll,\\n\\nI recently read your paper with Masoumehsadat Hosseini and Heiko M\u00fcller, \\\"Controlling the Rooms: How People Prefer Using Gestures to Control Their Smart Homes\\\" (CHI '24). Its frame-based elicitation of mid-air gestures across smart-home scenarios, aimed at gestures that stay consistent and transferable across devices, speaks directly to a question in my own work: how to develop culturally grounded mappings between visitors' gestures and programmable light in heritage exhibitions. Your group's research on ambient displays makes this connection even closer.\\n\\nI am preparing an application to the China Scholarship Council (CSC) for full funding of doctoral study starting in 2027, and I am writing to ask whether you would consider supervising my doctoral research in Media Informatics and Multimedia Systems at the University of Oldenburg.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\uff0810-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u53d1\u9001\uff0c\u53d1\u524d\u9010\u5c01\u786e\u8ba4\u3002\"}, \"unit_zh\": \"\u5965\u5c14\u767b\u5821\u5927\u5b66\u8ba1\u7b97\u79d1\u5b66\u7cfb\uff0c\u5a92\u4f53\u4fe1\u606f\u5b66\u4e0e\u591a\u5a92\u4f53\u7cfb\u7edf\u7ec4\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Harald Reiterer\", \"school_en\": \"Universit\u00e4t Konstanz\", \"school_zh\": \"\u5eb7\u65af\u5766\u8328\u5927\u5b66\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Prof. Dr. Mag.\uff0cProfessor\uff08\u81ea 2009 \u5e74\u4efb\u6b63\u6559\u6388\uff09\uff0cHCI Group \u8d1f\u8d23\u4eba\uff1b2019\u20132023 \u4efb\u7406\u5b66\u9662\u9662\u957f\", \"unit\": \"Human-Computer Interaction Group, Department of Computer and Information Science, University of Konstanz\", \"homepage\": \"https://hci.uni-konstanz.de/members/prof-dr-harald-reiterer/\", \"email\": \"Harald.Reiterer@uni-konstanz.de\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cB\u68af\u961f\u3011\u5168\u5fb7\u6700\u8d34\u8fd1\u300c\u4ea4\u4e92\u5c55\u89c8\u8bbe\u8ba1 + \u73b0\u573a\u90e8\u7f72 + \u8bbf\u5ba2\u6570\u636e\u8bc4\u4f30\u300d\u7684 HCI \u6559\u6388\uff1aMedia Exhibition Design \u8bfe\u7a0b\u6bcf\u5e74\u628a\u8ba1\u7b97\u673a\u3001\u8bbe\u8ba1\u3001\u5efa\u7b51\u3001\u5386\u53f2\u5b66\u751f\u505a\u6210\u771f\u5b9e\u5c55\u89c8\uff0c\u6b63\u597d\u5bf9\u5e94\u7528\u6237 RtD \u4e09\u9636\u6bb5\u4e2d\u7684\u73b0\u573a\u90e8\u7f72\uff1bCHI '26 \u8bba\u6587\u5f3a\u8c03\u5c55\u89c8\u7a7a\u95f4\u6574\u4f53\u4f53\u9a8c\uff0c\u4e0e\u300c\u7528\u5149\u4e32\u8054\u52a8\u4f5c\u2013\u5185\u5bb9\u2013\u7a7a\u95f4\u300d\u4e00\u81f4\u3002\u7f3a\u53e3\uff1a\u4e0d\u505a\u706f\u5149\u4e0e\u624b\u52bf\u8bc6\u522b\u672c\u8eab\uff0c\u7ec4\u89c4\u6a21\u5c0f\uff08\u5b98\u7f51 3 \u540d\u5728\u8bfb\u535a\u58eb\uff09\uff0c\u4e14\u9000\u4f11\u65f6\u95f4\u4e0d\u660e\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://hci.uni-konstanz.de/members/prof-dr-harald-reiterer/\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"Using Digital Twins to Design and Evaluate Interactive Exhibitions: A Case Study with Handheld AR\", \"year\": 2026, \"venue\": \"CHI '26 (Proceedings of the 2026 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems), Barcelona\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1145/3772318.3790852\", \"link_to_user\": \"\", \"title_zh\": \"\u5229\u7528\u6570\u5b57\u5b6a\u751f\u8bbe\u8ba1\u4e0e\u8bc4\u4f30\u4ea4\u4e92\u5c55\u89c8\uff1a\u624b\u6301 AR \u6848\u4f8b\u7814\u7a76\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://hci.uni-konstanz.de/members/prof-dr-harald-reiterer/\", \"https://hci.uni-konstanz.de/members/members\", \"https://hci.uni-konstanz.de/members/research-assistants/\", \"https://mediale-ausstellungsgestaltung.de/en/\", \"https://hci.uni-konstanz.de/research/research-projects/blended-museum\", \"https://kops.uni-konstanz.de/entities/publication/b61bbdd4-5e30-470f-9880-b640485277e2\", \"https://www.sfbtrr161.de/news/New-Exhibition-Arriving-Migration-Faith-and-Identity-Opens-in-Konstanz/?__locale=en\", \"https://www.uni-konstanz.de/studieren/rund-ums-studium/finanzen/studiengebuehren/studiengebuehren-fuer-internationale-studierende-und-fuer-ein-zweitstudium\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"Harald.Reiterer@uni-konstanz.de\", \"subject\": \"CSC-funded PhD enquiry (2027 entry): Gesture-driven narrative lighting for interactive exhibitions\", \"body\": \"Dear Professor Reiterer,\\n\\nI recently read your paper with Jonathan Wieland and colleagues, \\\"Using Digital Twins to Design and Evaluate Interactive Exhibitions: A Case Study with Handheld AR\\\" (CHI '26). Its argument that exhibits are still too often designed and experienced in isolation, and its use of a digital twin and interaction data from 1,303 visitors of \\\"Stayin' Alive\\\" to study the exhibition as a connected whole, resonate with my own aim: using light to link visitors' movements, content and space across an exhibition rather than at a single exhibit.\\n\\nI am preparing an application to the China Scholarship Council (CSC) for full funding of doctoral study starting in 2027, and I am writing to ask whether you would consider supervising my doctoral research in the Human-Computer Interaction Group at the University of Konstanz.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\uff0810-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u53d1\u9001\uff0c\u53d1\u524d\u9010\u5c01\u786e\u8ba4\u3002\"}, \"unit_zh\": \"\u5eb7\u65af\u5766\u8328\u5927\u5b66\u8ba1\u7b97\u673a\u4e0e\u4fe1\u606f\u79d1\u5b66\u7cfb\u4eba\u673a\u4ea4\u4e92\u7ec4\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Enrico Rukzio\", \"school_en\": \"Universit\u00e4t Ulm\", \"school_zh\": \"\u4e4c\u5c14\u59c6\u5927\u5b66\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Prof. Dr.\uff0cFull Professor of Human-Computer Interaction\uff0cHCI \u7ec4\u8d1f\u8d23\u4eba\uff0c\u5a92\u4f53\u7814\u7a76\u4e0e\u5a92\u4f53\u53d1\u5c55\u7814\u7a76\u6240\u6240\u957f\", \"unit\": \"Institute of Media Informatics, Human-Computer Interaction group, Ulm University\", \"homepage\": \"https://www.uni-ulm.de/in/mi/institut/personal/er/\", \"email\": \"enrico.rukzio@uni-ulm.de\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cC\u68af\u961f\u3011\u6b27\u6d32 HCI \u9876\u4f1a\u4ea7\u51fa\u6700\u591a\u7684\u7ec4\u4e4b\u4e00\uff0c\u957f\u671f\u505a\u624b\u52bf/XR/\u65b0\u4ea4\u4e92\u5e76\u5927\u91cf\u505a\u7528\u6237\u7814\u7a76\u4e0e\u5b9e\u5730\u6d4b\u8bd5\uff0c\u8fd1\u5e74\u5f00\u59cb\u505a\u8bbf\u5ba2\u53c2\u4e0e\uff08\u690d\u7269\u56ed\uff09\u4e0e\u706f\u5149\u63d0\u793a\u754c\u9762\uff0c\u53ef\u5bb9\u7eb3\u300c\u624b\u52bf\u9a71\u52a8\u53d9\u4e8b\u706f\u5149 + \u5bf9\u7167\u5b9e\u9a8c + \u73b0\u573a\u90e8\u7f72\u300d\uff1b\u4f46\u65e0\u535a\u7269\u9986/\u6587\u5316\u9057\u4ea7\u4e3b\u7ebf\uff0c\u706f\u5149\u4ec5\u4f5c\u4e3a\u6c7d\u8f66/\u8f85\u52a9\u573a\u666f\u7684\u8f93\u51fa\u6a21\u6001\uff0c\u504f\u5de5\u7a0b\u4e0e\u91cf\u5316\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://www.uni-ulm.de/in/mi/institut/personal/er/\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"BotaXplore: Enhancing Visitor Engagement and Learning in Botanical Gardens Through Mobile Technology\", \"year\": 2026, \"venue\": \"Extended Abstracts of the 2026 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems (CHI EA '26), 135:1\u2013135:5\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1145/3772363.3799272\", \"link_to_user\": \"\", \"title_zh\": \"BotaXplore\uff1a\u501f\u52a9\u79fb\u52a8\u6280\u672f\u63d0\u5347\u690d\u7269\u56ed\u6e38\u5ba2\u7684\u53c2\u4e0e\u5ea6\u4e0e\u5b66\u4e60\u6548\u679c\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://www.uni-ulm.de/in/mi/institut/personal/er/\", \"https://www.uni-ulm.de/en/in/mi/hci\", \"https://www.uni-ulm.de/en/in/mi/hci/publications/\", \"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3772363.3799272\", \"https://www.bibsonomy.org/bibtex/1cde038aa6e9c03daee7e4a4e30952125\", \"https://mwk.baden-wuerttemberg.de/de/hochschulen-studium/studieren-in-bw/studienfinanzierung/gebuehren-fuer-internationale-studierende-und-zweitstudium/faqs\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"enrico.rukzio@uni-ulm.de\", \"subject\": \"CSC-funded PhD enquiry (2027 entry): Gesture-driven narrative lighting for museum visitors\", \"body\": \"Dear Professor Rukzio,\\n\\nI recently read your paper with Albin Zeqiri and colleagues, \\\"BotaXplore: Enhancing Visitor Engagement and Learning in Botanical Gardens Through Mobile Technology\\\" (CHI EA '26). Its starting point, a focus group with botanists on designing tours that spark curiosity in heterogeneous audiences, and its three modes ranging from free exploration to tour-based visits, mirror a tension in my own work: how far a gesture-driven lighting system in a museum should guide visitors, and how much it should leave them free to explore.\\n\\nI am preparing an application to the China Scholarship Council (CSC) for full funding of doctoral study starting in 2027, and I am writing to ask whether you would consider supervising my doctoral research in the Human-Computer Interaction group at Ulm University.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\uff0810-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u53d1\u9001\uff0c\u53d1\u524d\u9010\u5c01\u786e\u8ba4\u3002\"}, \"unit_zh\": \"\u4e4c\u5c14\u59c6\u5927\u5b66\u5a92\u4f53\u4fe1\u606f\u5b66\u7814\u7a76\u6240\u4eba\u673a\u4ea4\u4e92\u7ec4\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Marc Erich Latoschik\", \"school_en\": \"Julius-Maximilians-Universit\u00e4t W\u00fcrzburg\", \"school_zh\": \"\u7ef4\u5c14\u8328\u5821\u5927\u5b66\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Prof. Dr.\uff0cHead of Chair for Human-Computer Interaction\uff08\u81ea 2011\uff09\uff1bXR Hub W\u00fcrzburg \u8054\u5408\u8d1f\u8d23\u4eba\", \"unit\": \"Chair for Human-Computer Interaction, University of W\u00fcrzburg\", \"homepage\": \"https://hci.uni-wuerzburg.de/people/marc-latoschik\", \"email\": \"marc.latoschik@uni-wuerzburg.de\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cC\u68af\u961f\u3011\u624b\u52bf\uff08\u591a\u6a21\u6001\u624b\u52bf\u4ea4\u4e92\u8d77\u5bb6\u3001\u73b0\u505a XR \u624b\u52bf\u751f\u6210\uff09+ \u5177\u8eab/\u4e34\u573a + \u53d9\u4e8b\u4f53\u9a8c\uff08TESDA\uff09\u4e09\u70b9\u4e0e\u7528\u6237\u8bfe\u9898\u76f8\u4ea4\uff0c\u5b9e\u9a8c\u65b9\u6cd5\u6210\u719f\uff1b\u4f46\u65e0\u6587\u5316\u9057\u4ea7/\u535a\u7269\u9986\u4e0e\u5b9e\u4f53\u706f\u5149\u7814\u7a76\uff0c\u8bfe\u9898\u9700\u4ee5\u300c\u6c89\u6d78\u4e0e\u624b\u52bf\u5bf9\u7a7a\u95f4\u4f53\u9a8c\u7684\u5f71\u54cd\u300d\u5207\u5165\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://hci.uni-wuerzburg.de/people/marc-latoschik\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"The Impact of AI-Based Real-Time Gesture Generation and Immersion on the Perception of Others and Interaction Quality in Social XR\", \"year\": 2025, \"venue\": \"IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics 31: 10131\u201310141\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1109/TVCG.2025.3616864\", \"link_to_user\": \"\", \"title_zh\": \"\u57fa\u4e8e AI \u7684\u5b9e\u65f6\u624b\u52bf\u751f\u6210\u4e0e\u6c89\u6d78\u611f\u5bf9\u793e\u4ea4 XR \u4e2d\u4ed6\u4eba\u611f\u77e5\u4e0e\u4ea4\u4e92\u8d28\u91cf\u7684\u5f71\u54cd\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://hci.uni-wuerzburg.de/people/marc-latoschik\", \"https://www.caidas.uni-wuerzburg.de/research-groups/human-computer-interaction/\", \"https://www.informatik.uni-wuerzburg.de/pis/research/publications/\", \"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/The-Impact-of-AI-Based-Real-Time-Gesture-Generation-Merz-Krome/956a3afaffffe465f65dfd12b48c0955a3248577\", \"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11189876\", \"https://www.uni-wuerzburg.de/grk3087\", \"https://www.mcm.uni-wuerzburg.de/fileadmin/10030500/2025/Open_PhD_positions_1__RTG_TESDA_final.pdf\", \"https://www.uni-wuerzburg.de/en/studying-at-jmu/studienangelegenheiten/application-and-enrolment/international-degree-seeking-students/before-arrival/costs-and-financing\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"marc.latoschik@uni-wuerzburg.de\", \"subject\": \"CSC-funded PhD enquiry (2027 entry): Gesture, immersion and narrative lighting in heritage exhibitions\", \"body\": \"Dear Professor Latoschik,\\n\\nI recently read your paper with Christian Merz and colleagues, \\\"The Impact of AI-Based Real-Time Gesture Generation and Immersion on the Perception of Others and Interaction Quality in Social XR\\\" (IEEE TVCG, 2025). Its finding that higher immersion strengthened presence and made the partner seem more human-like and believable, while the type of avatar animation did not significantly change conversation quality, raises a question I also face: when do gestures and their feedback really change how people experience a space, and when does immersion matter more?\\n\\nI am preparing an application to the China Scholarship Council (CSC) for full funding of doctoral study starting in 2027, and I am writing to ask whether you would consider supervising my doctoral research at the Chair of Human-Computer Interaction, University of W\u00fcrzburg.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\uff0810-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u53d1\u9001\uff0c\u53d1\u524d\u9010\u5c01\u786e\u8ba4\u3002\"}, \"title_zh\": \"\u6559\u6388\uff08Prof. Dr.\uff09\uff0c\u4eba\u673a\u4ea4\u4e92\u8bb2\u5e2d\u8d1f\u8d23\u4eba\uff08\u81ea 2011\uff09\uff1bXR Hub W\u00fcrzburg \u8054\u5408\u8d1f\u8d23\u4eba\", \"unit_zh\": \"\u7ef4\u5c14\u8328\u5821\u5927\u5b66\u4eba\u673a\u4ea4\u4e92\u8bb2\u5e2d\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Dr Paola Di Giuseppantonio Di Franco\", \"school_en\": \"Durham University\", \"school_zh\": \"\u675c\u4f26\u5927\u5b66\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Associate Professor (UKRI Future Leaders Fellow 2022\u20132026)\", \"unit\": \"Department of Geography (Faculty of Social Sciences and Health)\", \"homepage\": \"https://www.durham.ac.uk/departments/academic/arts-humanities/study/postgraduate-funding/phd-studentships-in-transformative-humanities/\", \"email\": \"paola.di-giuseppantonio-di-franco@durham.ac.uk\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cB\u68af\u961f\u3011\u6c89\u6d78\u5f0f\u9057\u4ea7+\u535a\u7269\u9986\u591a\u611f\u5b98\u4f53\u9a8c+\u5171\u521b/\u8fed\u4ee3\u8bbe\u8ba1\uff0c\u4e0e\u7533\u8bf7\u4eba\u7684\u9057\u4ea7\u53d9\u4e8b\u706f\u5149\u3001RtD \u548c\u539f\u4f4d\u90e8\u7f72\u9ad8\u5ea6\u5bf9\u5e94\uff1b\u5979 2025 \u8bba\u6587\u660e\u786e\u628a\u706f\u5149\u4e0e\u58f0\u666f\u5217\u4e3a\u865a\u62df\u5730\u65b9\u4f9d\u604b\u7684\u5173\u952e\u8981\u7d20\u3002\u7f3a\u53e3\uff1a\u4e0d\u505a\u624b\u52bf\u8bc6\u522b/\u53ef\u7f16\u7a0b\u706f\u5149\u786c\u4ef6\uff0c\u5b66\u79d1\u5728\u4eba\u6587\u5730\u7406/\u9057\u4ea7\u7814\u7a76\u800c\u975e\u8bbe\u8ba1/HCI\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/paola-di-giuseppantonio-di-franco/\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"Can immersive technologies rebuild heritage and sense of place? Examining Virtual Reality's role in fostering community resilience in post-disaster Italy\", \"year\": 2025, \"venue\": \"International Journal of Heritage Studies 31(7): 956\u2013977\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1080/13527258.2025.2520760\", \"link_to_user\": \"\", \"title_zh\": \"\u6c89\u6d78\u5f0f\u6280\u672f\u80fd\u5426\u91cd\u5efa\u9057\u4ea7\u4e0e\u5730\u65b9\u611f\uff1f\u63a2\u7a76\u865a\u62df\u73b0\u5b9e\u5728\u707e\u540e\u610f\u5927\u5229\u57f9\u80b2\u793e\u533a\u97e7\u6027\u4e2d\u7684\u4f5c\u7528\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://www.durham.ac.uk/departments/academic/arts-humanities/study/postgraduate-funding/phd-studentships-in-transformative-humanities/\", \"https://www.durham.ac.uk/research/institutes-and-centres/medical-humanities/about-us/news/2026/phd-studentships-in-transformative-humanities-at-durham-university/\", \"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/paola-di-giuseppantonio-di-franco/\", \"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13527258.2025.2520760\", \"https://socscihealth.webspace.durham.ac.uk/ (Geography in Faculty of Social Sciences and Health)\", \"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/c-l-h-warwick (backup lead supervisor)\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"active\uff082027 \u5165\u5b66\u622a\u6b62\u5df2\u89c1\uff1a2027-01-16\uff09\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"paola.di-giuseppantonio-di-franco@durham.ac.uk\", \"subject\": \"PhD enquiry (2027 entry): Transformative Humanities studentship \u2013 gesture-driven narrative lighting in heritage spaces\", \"body\": \"Dear Dr Di Giuseppantonio Di Franco,\\n\\nI recently read your paper \\\"Can immersive technologies rebuild heritage and sense of place? Examining Virtual Reality's role in fostering community resilience in post-disaster Italy\\\" (International Journal of Heritage Studies, 2025). I was struck by your finding that multi-sensory elements, especially lighting and soundscapes, were crucial for virtual place attachment, and that the team adjusted lighting when a night-time scene distressed a participant. My own work treats light as the narrative medium of a heritage space, so your iterative, community-centred approach speaks directly to how I hope to design and evaluate it with visitors.\\n\\nI am writing to ask whether you would consider supporting an application to the Durham PhD Studentships in Transformative Humanities for October 2027 entry, with you as lead supervisor and a co-supervisor from a second department, as the scheme requires.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\uff0810-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u53d1\u9001\uff0c\u53d1\u524d\u9010\u5c01\u786e\u8ba4\u3002\"}, \"title_zh\": \"\u526f\u6559\u6388\uff08UKRI \u672a\u6765\u9886\u8896\u5b66\u8005 2022\u20132026\uff09\", \"unit_zh\": \"\u5730\u7406\u7cfb\uff08\u793e\u4f1a\u79d1\u5b66\u4e0e\u5065\u5eb7\u5b66\u9662\uff09\"}, {\"name\": \"Dr Vlasios (Vlasis) Kasapakis\", \"school_en\": \"University of the Aegean\", \"school_zh\": \"\u7231\u7434\u6d77\u5927\u5b66\uff08\u5e0c\u814a\uff0c\u7c73\u8482\u5229\u5c3c\uff09\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Associate Professor (tenured), Extended Reality; Director of XR-Lab\", \"unit\": \"Department of Cultural Technology and Communication, University of the Aegean\", \"homepage\": \"https://xrlab.ct.aegean.gr/\", \"email\": \"v.kasapakis@aegean.gr\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cD\u68af\u961f\u3011\u9057\u4ea7 XR + \u4ea4\u4e92\u53d9\u4e8b + \u624b\u90e8\u8ffd\u8e2a\u4ea4\u4e92\u8bc4\u4f30\uff0c\u4e0e\u7533\u8bf7\u4eba\u624b\u52bf\u4ea4\u4e92\u3001\u6566\u714c/\u9752\u94dc\u5668 XR \u539f\u578b\u3001HoloLens 2 \u7ecf\u5386\u76f4\u63a5\u5bf9\u5e94\uff1b\u7f3a\u53e3\uff1a\u4e0d\u505a\u706f\u5149/\u5b9e\u4f53\u5149\uff0c\u6280\u672f\u5bfc\u5411\u504f CS\uff08Unity/C#\uff09\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://xrlab.ct.aegean.gr/\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"Hand Tracking vs Motion Controllers: The Effects on Immersive Virtual Reality Game Experience\", \"year\": 2022, \"venue\": \"2022 IEEE International Symposium on Multimedia (ISM), pp. 206\u2013207\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1109/ISM55400.2022.00045\", \"link_to_user\": \"\", \"title_zh\": \"\u624b\u90e8\u8ffd\u8e2a\u4e0e\u8fd0\u52a8\u63a7\u5236\u5668\u4e4b\u6bd4\u8f83\uff1a\u5bf9\u6c89\u6d78\u5f0f\u865a\u62df\u73b0\u5b9e\u6e38\u620f\u4f53\u9a8c\u7684\u5f71\u54cd\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://xrlab.ct.aegean.gr/\", \"https://xrlab.ct.aegean.gr/publications.html\", \"https://ct.aegean.gr/en/the-department-establishes-the-new-extended-reality-laboratory-xr-lab/\", \"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/vlasis-kasapakis-3911378b_phd-postdoc-virtualreality-activity-7512173156371959809-ExYE\", \"https://www.applykite.com/positions/phdpostdoc-positions-in-vrar-development-for-digital-cultural-heritage-9bxynpe0l1\", \"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/ism/NeamonitiK22.html\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"v.kasapakis@aegean.gr\", \"subject\": \"PhD enquiry (2027 entry): VR/AR for digital cultural heritage \u2013 gesture-driven narrative lighting\", \"body\": \"Dear Dr Kasapakis,\\n\\nI recently read your paper with Sophia Neamoniti, \\\"Hand Tracking vs Motion Controllers: The Effects on Immersive Virtual Reality Game Experience\\\" (IEEE ISM 2022). Its finding that hand tracking showed lower usability and learnability than motion controllers, without reducing the overall game experience, is directly relevant to my work: my installations rely on camera-based hand and body gestures instead of controllers, and they must remain easy to learn for first-time museum visitors.\\n\\nI saw your recent call for PhD researchers in VR/AR development for digital cultural heritage at XR-Lab, and I am writing to ask whether a doctoral project in this area could fit within it, starting by September 2027.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\uff0810-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff09\uff0c\u672a\u53d1\u9001\uff0c\u53d1\u524d\u9010\u5c01\u786e\u8ba4\u3002\"}, \"title_zh\": \"\u526f\u6559\u6388\uff08\u7ec8\u8eab\u6559\u804c\uff09\uff0c\u6269\u5c55\u73b0\u5b9e\u65b9\u5411\uff1bXR-Lab \u4e3b\u4efb\", \"unit_zh\": \"\u7231\u7434\u6d77\u5927\u5b66\u6587\u5316\u6280\u672f\u4e0e\u4f20\u64ad\u7cfb\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Thomas Pearce\", \"school_en\": \"Bauhaus-Universit\u00e4t Weimar\", \"school_zh\": \"\u9b4f\u739b\u5305\u8c6a\u65af\u5927\u5b66\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"Jun.-Prof. Dr. (Junior Professor, tenure track since 2022-09; PhD Architectural Design, Bartlett UCL 2022)\", \"unit\": \"Faculty of Art and Design \u2013 Emerging Technologies and Design (EmTaD), Product Design\", \"homepage\": \"https://www.uni-weimar.de/en/art-and-design/chairs/emerging-technologies-and-design/people/team/thomas-pearce/\", \"email\": \"thomas.pearce@uni-weimar.de\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cB\u68af\u961f\u3011\u70b9\u4e91/\u6444\u5f71\u6d4b\u91cf\u91cd\u5efa\u6587\u5316\u9057\u4ea7\u7a7a\u95f4\u3001\u6df7\u5408\u73b0\u5b9e\u8bfe\u7a0b\u3001\u8eab\u4f53\u8868\u6f14\u8bbe\u8ba1\uff0c\u4e0e\u7533\u8bf7\u4eba\u70b9\u4e91\u7c92\u5b50\u9057\u4ea7\u539f\u578b\u548c MR \u7ecf\u5386\u76f4\u63a5\u76f8\u5173\uff1bDr. phil. \u8def\u7ebf\u65e0\u8bed\u8a00\u8bc1\u4e66\u8981\u6c42\uff1b\u706f\u5149\u4e0e\u624b\u52bf\u4ea4\u4e92\u975e\u5176\u4e3b\u4e1a\uff0c\u62df Hesselmeier \u4f5c\u7b2c\u4e8c\u5bfc\u5e08\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://www.uni-weimar.de/en/art-and-design/chairs/emerging-technologies-and-design/people/team/thomas-pearce/\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"Measuring Adolf Loos' Parallax: Retroactive Photogrammetry and the Persistent Off-Screen\", \"year\": 2024, \"venue\": \"ARENA Journal of Architectural Research 9(1)\", \"title_zh\": \"\u6d4b\u91cf Adolf Loos \u7684\u89c6\u5dee\uff1a\u56de\u6eaf\u5f0f\u6444\u5f71\u6d4b\u91cf\u4e0e\u6301\u7eed\u7684\u753b\u5916\u7a7a\u95f4\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://www.uni-weimar.de/en/art-and-design/chairs/emerging-technologies-and-design/people/team/thomas-pearce/\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"thomas.pearce@uni-weimar.de\", \"subject\": \"CSC-funded PhD enquiry (2027 entry): Gesture-driven narrative lighting for digital heritage\", \"body\": \"Dear Professor Pearce,\\n\\nI recently read your paper \\\"Measuring Adolf Loos' Parallax: Retroactive Photogrammetry and the Persistent Off-Screen\\\" in the ARENA Journal of Architectural Research. By using the 1901 photographs of Loos' mirror-lined Viennese tailor's shop as an unintended source for photogrammetric reconstruction, you recover the shop and its staged figures as a point cloud, yet show that the reconstruction produces new forms of the immeasurable. This resonates with my own work: I sample point clouds from heritage objects and let visitors' gestures set them in motion, and I want to understand how light, reflection and the viewer's position shape what such reconstructions can convey.\\n\\nI hope to begin a doctorate in autumn 2027 with funding from the China Scholarship Council (CSC). Given your chair's work on digital capture, design for performance and speculative design historiographies, I would like to ask whether you would consider supervising my doctorate (Dr. phil.) at the Faculty of Art and Design, possibly together with a second supervisor working on light and interaction.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"Dr. phil.\uff08\u827a\u672f\u4e0e\u8bbe\u8ba1\u5b66\u9662\uff09\u8def\u7ebf\uff1b\u672a\u70b9\u540d Hesselmeier\uff1bPearce \u56de\u590d\u79ef\u6781\u540e\u518d\u8054\u7cfb\u7b2c\u4e8c\u5bfc\u5e08\uff1bMona Mahall \u4e3a\u5907\u9009\uff0c\u7b49\u56de\u590d\u518d\u5b9a\u3002\"}, \"title_zh\": \"\u9752\u5e74\u6559\u6388\uff08Jun.-Prof. Dr.\uff0c2022-09 \u8d77\u7ec8\u8eab\u8f68\uff1b\u4f26\u6566\u5927\u5b66\u5b66\u9662\u5df4\u7279\u83b1\u7279\u5efa\u7b51\u5b66\u9662\u5efa\u7b51\u8bbe\u8ba1\u535a\u58eb\uff0c2022\uff09\", \"unit_zh\": \"\u827a\u672f\u4e0e\u8bbe\u8ba1\u5b66\u9662 \u2013 \u65b0\u5174\u6280\u672f\u4e0e\u8bbe\u8ba1\uff08EmTaD\uff09\uff0c\u4ea7\u54c1\u8bbe\u8ba1\", \"csc_status_zh\": \"\u672a\u77e5\"}, {\"name\": \"Alexander Wiethoff\", \"school_en\": \"Ludwig-Maximilians-Universit\u00e4t M\u00fcnchen (LMU)\", \"school_zh\": \"\u6155\u5c3c\u9ed1\u5927\u5b66\uff08LMU\uff09\", \"country\": \"\", \"title\": \"APL Prof. Dr., Media Informatics / HCI\", \"unit\": \"Institut f\u00fcr Informatik, LMU M\u00fcnchen\", \"homepage\": \"https://www.medien.ifi.lmu.de/team/alexander.wiethoff/\", \"email\": \"alexander.wiethoff@ifi.lmu.de\", \"relevance\": null, \"claim\": \"\u3010\u7b2c\u4e5d\u6279\u00b710-13 \u5f85\u53d1\uff5cB\u68af\u961f\u3011\u4ea4\u4e92\u7167\u660e\u3001\u5a92\u4f53\u5efa\u7b51\u3001\u5177\u8eab\u706f\u5149\u4ea4\u4e92\uff08StarLight\uff09\u3001\u59ff\u6001\u63a7\u706f\u4e0e\u706f\u5149\u663e\u793a\u539f\u578b\u4e3a\u5176\u4ee3\u8868\u4f5c\uff0c\u8bbe\u8ba1\u80cc\u666f\u3001RtD \u5f0f\u539f\u578b\u4e0e\u91ce\u5916\u90e8\u7f72\uff0c\u5bf9 M.F.A.+\u7167\u660e\u4ea7\u54c1\u7ecf\u7406\u80cc\u666f\u53cb\u597d\uff1b\u9057\u4ea7/\u535a\u7269\u9986\u975e\u4e3b\u7ebf\uff0c\u8fd1\u4e09\u5e74\u4ea7\u51fa\u5c11\u3002\", \"evidence_homepage\": \"https://www.medien.ifi.lmu.de/team/alexander.wiethoff/\", \"evidence_papers\": [{\"title\": \"StarLight \u2013 Exploring Embodied Interactions with Media Architecture and Large Public Audiences\", \"year\": 2015, \"venue\": \"PerDis 2015 (ACM)\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1145/2757710.2757726\", \"title_zh\": \"StarLight \u2013 \u63a2\u7d22\u4e0e\u5a92\u4f53\u5efa\u7b51\u53ca\u5927\u89c4\u6a21\u516c\u4f17\u89c2\u4f17\u7684\u5177\u8eab\u4ea4\u4e92\"}], \"evidence_projects_funding\": null, \"fit_to_user\": null, \"counterargument_risk\": null, \"email_hook\": null, \"sources\": [\"https://www.medien.ifi.lmu.de/team/alexander.wiethoff/\"], \"verified\": false, \"csc_note\": \"\", \"matched_keywords\": [], \"csc_status\": \"unknown\", \"in_user_csc_list\": false, \"email_draft\": {\"to\": \"alexander.wiethoff@ifi.lmu.de\", \"subject\": \"CSC-funded PhD enquiry (2027 entry): gesture-driven interactive lighting for museum heritage\", \"body\": \"Dear Professor Wiethoff,\\n\\nI recently read your paper \\\"StarLight \u2013 Exploring Embodied Interactions with Media Architecture and Large Public Audiences\\\" (PerDis '15), which presents an interactive lighting system studied in the wild at a live music festival and reports how people perceived interacting with light in front of a large public audience, using several UX evaluation methods in parallel. It speaks directly to a question in my own work: how visitors' bodily movements, translated into programmable light, can shape the way they encounter cultural heritage in an exhibition space. Your work on low-resolution lighting displays and on prototyping interactive light makes this connection even closer.\\n\\nI am preparing an application to the LMU\u2013CSC Scholarship Program, through which the China Scholarship Council (CSC) would fully fund a doctorate at LMU starting in 2027, and I am writing to ask whether you would consider supervising my doctoral research in Media Informatics.\\n\\nI direct the Digital Intangible Cultural Heritage Design and Production Teaching and Research Office at Quanzhou Huaguang College, where I teach 3D character design and digital creative product design. I hold a B.A. in Product Design from Hunan University of Technology Science and Technology College (average 80/100) and an M.F.A. in Digital Art Design from Jiangsu University (average 85/100). Beyond my degrees, I bring two years as a lighting hardware product manager at LEEDARSON and OSRAM/LEDVANCE, taking products from user research to mass production. I have also built gesture-controlled particle prototypes of Chinese bronzes and Dunhuang statues and, for my master's research, a HoloLens 2 mixed-reality system for customising recreational-vehicle interiors, tested with users.\\n\\nVideos and details of these projects are on my homepage: https://cooleli.github.io/CV-project/v2/\\n\\nI have attached my CV and a short research proposal. It outlines a Research through Design study of gesture-driven narrative lighting, using camera-based gesture recognition and programmable lighting to link visitors' movements, heritage content and the exhibition space, with Dunhuang murals and traditional Chinese patterns as cases, across design exploration, a controlled experiment and in-situ deployment. I would be grateful to know whether this topic could fit within your supervision.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nHanlei (Eli) Zeng\\nQuanzhou Huaguang College, China\", \"note_zh\": \"\u66ff\u6362 Butz\uff08\u660e\u5e74\u9000\u4f11\uff09\uff1b\u4fe1\u4e2d\u672a\u63d0 Butz\u3002\"}");